spec:
  grid: 14-19 rows x 13-19 cols, background 0
  blocks:
    count: 1-3 solid 3x3 same-color squares (cross generators)
    colors: distinct per block, drawn from 1-9
    separation: center rows pairwise differ by >2, center cols pairwise differ by >2 [observed >=3 row, >=4 col]
    placement: block edges may touch grid border (margin >= 0)
  noise:
    density: 5-12% of grid cells, scattered as mostly isolated single pixels
    colors: any from 1-9 including block colors; each same-color 4-connected noise component has size <= 2 [observed]
    distribution: spread across the grid, may be adjacent to blocks
  output_rule: |
    For each 3x3 block with center (r,c) and color C:
      fill entire row r and entire column c with C.
    Then for every pair of distinct blocks (i,j):
      reset pixel (row_i, col_j) to background.
    Noise pixels off the cross lines are preserved; noise on cross lines is overwritten.

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct (input-first) -- output is deterministic from input
  steps:
    1. Pick grid H in [14,19], W in [13,19].
    2. Pick N blocks in [1,3]. Choose N distinct colors from 1-9.
    3. Place N block centers ensuring pairwise |row_diff|>2 and |col_diff|>2, each center at least 1 cell from edge (so 3x3 fits). Use rejection or greedy placement.
    4. Fill 3x3 solid squares at each center with its color on a bg=0 grid.
    5. Scatter noise pixels (5-12% of total cells) at random empty positions (not inside any 3x3 block). Each pixel gets a random color from 1-9. Ensure no same-color 4-connected component among noise exceeds size 2.
```
