spec:
  grid: 3-5 rows x 8-12 cols; background always black (0)
  outline:
    color: single non-bg, non-red color (any from {1,3,4,6,8}) [observed]
    structure: 2-4 diagonal segments (slope exactly +/-1), each length 2-5 pixels
    apexes: 1-2 start points, always on row 0 (one may be on row 1) [observed]
    connectivity: every pixel connects diagonally to a neighbor above or below; segments form a tree rooted at apexes
    coverage: every row has >=1 outline pixel; outline spans all rows
    row_constraint: >=2 rows have >=2 outline pixels (to ensure filling occurs)
    gap: min horizontal gap between consecutive outline pixels in any row is 2
    between consecutive outline pixels in same row, all cells are background
  fill: recolor background pixels strictly between each consecutive pair of outline pixels per row to red (2)
  padding: 0-2 empty columns may exist to the right of rightmost outline pixel [observed]

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction of diagonal segment tree
  steps:
    1. Pick grid rows R in [3,5], outline_color from {1,3,4,5,6,7,8,9} minus {2}.
    2. Place 1-2 apex pixels on row 0 (or rarely row 0 and row 1).
    3. From each apex, extend 1-2 diagonal arms downward (slope +/-1), each arm length 1 to R-1 steps. At least one arm per apex must have length >=1.
    4. Arms may merge at a shared leaf point (two arms from different apexes converge). Ensure no two outline pixels occupy the same cell.
    5. Verify every row has >=1 outline pixel and at least one row has >=2 (guaranteeing fill). Verify min horizontal gap >=2. Verify all non-outline cells in spans are background.
    6. Set grid width = max_outline_col + 1 + randint(0,2) for optional right padding.
    7. Fill all non-outline cells on the grid with background (0).
